  "ended_on_llm_error": false,
  "final_message": "I've built the bank: a Flask API in `backend/app.py` and a React + Tailwind frontend in `frontend/src/`. I ran the API under gunicorn and tested it with a script covering every endpoint, and the frontend type-checks and builds. I couldn't build or run the Docker image because Docker isn't available here, and I didn't click through the frontend in a browser.\n\n**What the tests showed:**\n- Registering answers 201, and a duplicate username gets 409. Login returns `{\"token\": ...}`, and any call without a valid token gets 401.\n- Each of these is refused with a clear message, which the confirmation step shows to the user: insufficient balance, an unknown recipient, sending to yourself, a zero or negative amount, and more than two decimal places.\n- I sent 20 transfers of 100 from one account at the same time. Exactly 9 went through, the rest were refused for insufficient balance, and the two balances still added up. Each transfer is one all-or-nothing database transaction, and money is stored as whole cents.\n- Paging returns `items`, `total`, `page` and `page_size`, newest first. A user who wasn't part of a transfer gets 404 when asking for it.\n\n**Behaviour you might not expect:**\n- **Anti-forgery token:** if a request sends an `X-CSRF-Token` header, it must be correct or the request gets 403. If the header is missing, the request is still accepted, since the bearer token is what identifies the user. The frontend always sends it.\n- **Validation limits I chose:** usernames are 3\u201364 characters (letters, digits, `.`, `_`, `-`) and not case-sensitive, passwords need at least 6 characters, and memos are capped at 200 characters. `page_size` is capped at 100 and defaults to 20.\n- **Sign-in tokens** last 7 days. The frontend keeps the token in the browser tab's session storage, so closing the tab signs you out.\n- **Data file:** the database is `./data/bank.sqlite3`; the `DATA_DIR` environment variable can point it elsewhere.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- **`Dockerfile`:** the pip install step now uses `--require-hashes -r backend/requirements.lock`. The original constraints-file form failed with an older pip (25.1).\n- **New files:** `frontend/tsconfig.json`, `src/index.css` (Tailwind's entry file only) and a `.gitignore`. `package.json` now pins exact versions and has a `typecheck` script.\n- **`README.md`:** I added a short section about the app.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
